  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nBroad surface high pressure today keeps the boundary layer flow\nlight. Low-level flow transitions to southwesterly by \nWednesday. This will allow temperatures to gradually warm, with\nafternoon readings by Thursday in the 80s for all but the \nhigher elevations.\n\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA cold front will then push southward into the region on Friday,\nbringing chances of showers, and possibly thunderstorms. Models\nthen diverge on where the front stalls out, with some taking the\nfront south of the region and other leaving it over the area. \nThis is critical to the forecast over the weekend. If the front\ngoes south of the area, the best moisture and instability would\nstay south of the region. If the front were to stall over the\narea, heavier rainfall would become a possibility.",
